TSPIN two-spin dipole validation
================================

The in.spin.tspin_dipole input is a deterministic two-atom test of coupled
lattice and variable-magnitude spin dynamics.  It uses only styles from the
LAMMPS SPIN package:

  pair_style spin/dipole/cut
  fix spring/tspin
  fix nve/tspin

Analytic reference
------------------

For two complete spin vectors S1 and S2 separated by r with unit separation
vector e, the pair energy is

  U = C/r^3 [ S1.S2 - 3(S1.e)(S2.e) ],

where

  C = mu_0 mu_B^2/(4 pi) = 5.3668995380683553e-5 eV Angstrom^3.

The example uses

  r  = 1.5 Angstrom,
  S1 = 2 (1/sqrt(2), 1/sqrt(2), 0),
  S2 = 3 (0.6, 0, 0.8).

The exact pair energy is

  U = -8.0959382556055094e-5 eV.

The complete Cartesian magnetic force on spin 1 is

  -dU/dS1 = ( 5.7246928406062451e-5,
               0,
              -3.8164618937374974e-5 ) eV/mu_B.

Its projection along the direction of S1 is nonzero,

  s1.(-dU/dS1) = 4.0479691278027547e-5 eV/mu_B,

which explicitly tests the longitudinal force that changes the spin modulus.
With hbar = 6.5821191017147152e-4 eV ps/rad, the corresponding LAMMPS
magnetic-force array is

  fm1 = |S1|/hbar (-dU/dS1)
      = ( 0.17394680199921933,
          0,
         -0.11596453466614624 ) rad.THz.

The exact mechanical force on atom 1 is

  F1 = ( 1.6191876511211020e-4,
        -8.0959382556055110e-5,
        -1.0794584340807350e-4 ) eV/Angstrom.

Permanent unit test
-------------------

TSpinTest.DipoleCutProvidesFullGradient checks all of the following:

1. The LAMMPS pair energy equals the closed-form value above.
2. hbar/|S1| times fm1 equals the analytic -dU/dS1.
3. Every component agrees with an independent central finite difference of
   the LAMMPS energy with respect to the Cartesian components of S1.
4. The atom force agrees with both its closed form and a central finite
   difference with respect to the atom position.
5. The longitudinal projection of the spin force is nonzero.

Dynamic convergence
-------------------

The input accepts command-line overrides for dt and nsteps.  These runs cover
the same physical duration of 2 ps:

  lmp -var dt 0.001   -var nsteps 2000 -in in.spin.tspin_dipole
  lmp -var dt 0.0005  -var nsteps 4000 -in in.spin.tspin_dipole
  lmp -var dt 0.00025 -var nsteps 8000 -in in.spin.tspin_dipole

For the current implementation, the absolute final drift in etotal+c_ske is

  dt (ps)       absolute drift (eV)
  0.001         8.1813582059e-12
  0.0005        2.0452963054e-12
  0.00025       5.1131980052e-13

The error decreases by a factor of about four whenever the timestep is
halved, as expected for velocity-Verlet integration.  The complete thermo
tables are also identical between one and four MPI ranks for this case.
